    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification side-effect on successful owner create in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:110`) alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n\n2. **Added the `enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner)` helper** that emits a line on the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and the member id. The member id is resolved through the existing `primaryIdentifier(owner)` accessor, matching how the audit trail already resolves it.\n\n3. **Wired it into the create pipeline** \u2014 called from `createOwner(...)` immediately after `auditOwnerCreated(...)`, so it fires only on a successful create (after persistence and mapping), mirroring the placement of the audit side-effect.\n\nThe emitted line looks like:\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification: ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```\n\nThis satisfies the spec (a `NOTIFY` line carrying both the owner id and the memberId). The `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
